\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T16:06:59-07:00","id":99564,"title":"","content":"It is possible that once the original 5 are done with the 20th anniversary editions, the newer games like Hunter and Demon might see 15th anniversaries instead. Or OP might just not care about the &quot;real&quot; numbers since we've kind of blown past them (WtA 2012, Mage 2013, Wraith 2014, Changeling 2015) for at least Werewolf and Mage already. If Wr20 gets done before the end of the year it might get things back on track though.<br /> <br /> The games that never got stand-alone books (KotE, Mummy) seem a bit more up in the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}